From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:09:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] west.yml: Zephyr 4.5.0 and zephyrproject-rtos xenlib

Move the Dom0 west pins to upstream Zephyr v4.5.0 and switch zephyr-xenlib to
its upstream at zephyrproject-rtos.

xen-troops/zephyr has no branch for 4.5, so zephyr is pinned to the upstream
tag itself. Nothing is lost by leaving the fork: the zephyr-v4.4.1-xt branch
this series used before is upstream v4.4.1 at the same SHA (1f6485eca254).

fatfs has to move with Zephyr: modules/fatfs/zephyr_fatfs_config.h asserts
`FFCONF_DEF == 80386`, which the original pin (80286) fails. 4f60a12c is what
v4.5.0's own west.yml points at: FatFs R0.16 with upstream patches 1 and 2 and
the fixes for CVE-2026-6682, -6683, -6685, -6686 and -6687.

zephyr-xenlib stays at 7f088456. v4.5.0's own west.yml names a newer xenlib
(8b13d0b7), but its xenstore server was reworked there and seven of the eleven
xenlib patches in this series no longer apply. v4.5.0 builds against 7f088456
(every Xen public header it includes is there), so moving xenlib is left to a
change of its own. zephyr-xrun is unchanged too.

moulin's west source can only pin the manifest repository's url/rev, so the
project pins can only be changed by patching this file - which is why this
patch is applied first and `west update` is then re-run (see apply-zephyr-
patches.sh).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-dom0-xt]
---
diff --git a/west.yml b/west.yml
index fdc0ac8..4bbb0c2 100644
--- a/west.yml
+++ b/west.yml
@@ -12,16 +12,28 @@ manifest:
       url-base: https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/
 
   projects:
+    # Pins are SHAs, not branch/tag names: a branch name makes the build
+    # irreproducible (it changes the moment upstream moves) and unreviewable in
+    # a PR. The symbolic name each SHA came from is in the comment.
+    # xen-troops has no branch for Zephyr 4.5, so this pins the upstream tag
+    # directly.
     - name: zephyr
-      remote: xentroops
-      revision: f12d445f792d562f23c107379267f07674ab5ebd
+      remote: zephyrproject-rtos
+      revision: 41d10b59730406bbab4ca9f1fbbe9e96aafb4966  # v4.5.0
       west-commands: scripts/west-commands.yml
+    # zephyrproject-rtos is the upstream for xenlib now; xen-troops/zephyr-xenlib
+    # is a mirror. The upstream side carries no tags at all, so the old `v3.2.0`
+    # tag cannot be expressed here - this pin is a main commit.
     - name: zephyr-xenlib
-      remote: xentroops
-      revision: v3.2.0
+      remote: zephyrproject-rtos
+      revision: 7f0884563f865a2a223f26dd0d847fb0faad397d  # main
+    # Must track what this Zephyr expects: modules/fatfs/zephyr_fatfs_config.h
+    # has `#if FFCONF_DEF != 80386`, and the original pin (427159bf) is
+    # FF_DEFINED 80286 -> hard compile error. 4f60a12c is what v4.5.0's own
+    # west.yml points at (FatFs R0.16 with upstream patches 1-2).
     - name: fatfs
       remote: zephyrproject-rtos
-      revision: 427159bf95ea49b7680facffaa29ad506b42709b
+      revision: 4f60a12c58c3de4246857ad87c40239ecd93349b  # v4.5.0 west.yml
     - name: zephyr-xrun
       remote: xentroops
-      revision: 5b6ecf274bac79b0be740693766a88d3eedf3b44
+      revision: 5b6ecf274bac79b0be740693766a88d3eedf3b44  # v0.1.0, unchanged
